Falsifies `generational_table::verification::the_walk_bound_and_the_live_count_survive_any_operation`.

The defect: insert raises the walk bound only when the slot it fills is strictly above it, an off
by one in the one place the bound grows. First-fit fills the slot at `top` whenever every slot
below it is live, so a table filled from empty never raises its bound past zero, and every walk
bounded by it misses the entry it just took.

Expected to fail: the harness's assertion that no live entry sits above the walk bound, after an
insert into a table whose free slot is the one at `top`.
